Accessibility > automatic QTE (the live GOW_QTE_AUTO / F1 toggle, default off) also performs recognized stick gestures,
as requested by the maintainer after the cabin minigame test. While a zzz-332 rotation guide is fresh, the left stick of
every pad read (keyboard and controller, and the keyboard packet path) follows the guide: half turns repeat
start > 180-degree arc the guide's way > hold > release every 0.6 s; full turns keep turning the guide's way at two
turns per second. Time-based (repeated reads agree), restarted when the guide changes, inactive without focus, in
scripted pad tests and with GOW_QTE_KEY_SWEEP=0. Unknown/wiggle prompts stay manual. The F1 menu text says buttons and
stick. Tests: qte_hold_test (cycle, direction, release, restart), control-prompts auto mode (production reader,
focus loss, live toggle).

